  "term": "competency to stand trial",
  "definition": "In forensic psychology and psychiatry, competency to stand trial is a legally important question that may be examined in an evaluation for the court. It refers to whether a person is considered able to undergo trial, although the packet does not give the specific standards used to decide this.",
